*** {{tact|end}}
* {{topt|Can you give me any farming advice?}}
** '''Player:''' Can you give me any farming advice?
** {{trandom}}
** {{topt|Dialogue 1}}
*** '''Alexandra:''' You can put up to five tomatoes, strawberries, apples, bananas or oranges into a fruit basket, although you can't have a mix in the same basket.
*** {{tact|initial}}
** {{topt|Dialogue 2}}
*** '''Alexandra:''' There are seven main Farming areas - Elstan's area near Falador, Dantaera's area near Catherby, Kragen's area near Ardougne, Lyra's area in Morytania, Marisi's area in Hosidius, Alan's area in the Farming Guild and
*** '''Alexandra:''' Oswallt's area in Prifddinas.
*** {{tact|initial}}
** {{topt|Dialogue 3}}
*** '''Alexandra:''' Supercompost is far better than normal compost, but more expensive to make. You need to rot the right type of item; show me an item, and I'll tell you if it's super- compostable or not.
*** {{tact|initial}}
** {{topt|Dialogue 4}}
*** '''Alexandra:''' Vegetables, hops and flowers need constant watering - if you ignore my advice, you will sooner or later find yourself in possession of a dead farming patch.
*** {{tact|initial}}
** {{topt|Dialogue 5}}
*** '''Alexandra:''' There is a special patch for growing Belladonna - I believe that it is somewhere near Draynor Manor, where the ground is a tad 'unblessed'.
*** {{tact|initial}}
** {{topt|Dialogue 6}}
*** '''Alexandra:''' Hops are good for brewing ales. I believe there's a brewery up in Keldagrim somewhere, and I've heard rumours that a place called Phasmatys used to be good for that type of thing. 'Fore they all died, of course.
*** {{tact|initial}}
** {{topt|Dialogue 7}}
*** '''Alexandra:''' Bittercap mushrooms can only be grown in a special patch in Morytania, near the Mort Myre swamp. There the ground is especially dank and suited to growing poisonous fungii.
*** {{tact|initial}}
** {{topt|Dialogue 8}}
*** '''Alexandra:''' You can buy all the farming tools from farming shops, which can be found close to the allotments.
*** {{tact|initial}}
** {{topt|Dialogue 9}}
*** '''Alexandra:''' Tree seeds must be grown in a plantpot of soil into a sapling, and then transferred to a tree patch to continue growing to adulthood.
*** {{tact|initial}}
** {{topt|Dialogue 10}}
*** '''Alexandra:''' The only way to cure a bush or tree of disease is to prune away the diseased leaves with a pair of secateurs. For all other crops I would just apply some plant-cure.
*** {{tact|initial}}
** {{topt|Dialogue 11}}
*** '''Alexandra:''' You can fill plantpots with soil from any empty patch, if you have a gardening trowel.
*** {{tact|initial}}
** {{topt|Dialogue 12}}
*** '''Alexandra:''' If you need to be rid of your fruit trees for any reason, all you have to do is chop them down and then dig up the stump.
*** {{tact|initial}}
** {{topt|Dialogue 13}}
*** '''Alexandra:''' Don't just throw away your weeds after you've raked a patch - put them in a compost bin and make some compost.
*** {{tact|initial}}
** {{topt|Dialogue 14}}
*** '''Alexandra:''' Applying compost to a patch will not only reduce the chance that your crops will get diseased, but you will also grow more crops to harvest.
*** {{tact|initial}}
** {{topt|Dialogue 15}}
*** '''Alexandra:''' If you want to make your own sacks and baskets you'll need to use the loom that's near the Farming shop in Falador. If you're a good enough craftsman, that is.
*** {{tact|initial}}
** {{topt|Dialogue 16}}
*** '''Alexandra:''' You don't have to buy all your plantpots you know, you can make them yourself on a pottery wheel. If you're a good enough craftsman, that is.
*** {{tact|initial}}
** {{topt|Dialogue 17}}
*** '''Alexandra:''' You can put up to ten potatoes, cabbages or onions in vegetable sacks, although you can't have a mix in the same sack.
*** {{tact|initial}}
* {{topt|Can you sell me something?}}
** '''Player:''' Can you sell me something?
** '''Alexandra:''' That depends on whether I have it to sell. What is it that you're looking for?
** {{tact|opens=Farming Supplies}}
* {{topt|I'll come back another time.}}
** '''Player:''' I'll come back another time.
** {{tact|end}}

