===Subsequent times===
* '''Player:''' Hello!
* '''Chartin' Charles McAtless:''' Good day!
* {{tselect|Select an option}}
* {{topt|How do I go about charting the sea?}}
** '''Player:''' How do I go about charting the sea?
** '''Chartin' Charles McAtless:''' Well, that very much depends. You see, when it comes to charting, there are quite a few different things you'll want to track. What you need to do is going to vary depending on what it is you're tracking.
** '''Chartin' Charles McAtless:''' That said, the starting point is always going to be your captain's log. I actually helped author the standard log that we give out around the Pandemonium.
** '''Chartin' Charles McAtless:''' I made sure to include some big hints in there about the things you might find on your sailing adventures.
** {{tbox|You get the distinct impression you were just winked at by a blindfolded eye.}}
** '''Player:''' You say there are a few different things I might want to track. What are they?
** '''Chartin' Charles McAtless:''' Well, you have both big and small points of interest, water currents, sea depths, weather patterns, and then there's also drink crates. They're a curious one that Steve likes people to track.
** {{tselect|Select an option}}
** {{topt|Can you tell me about charting smaller points of interest?}}
*** '''Player:''' Can you tell me about charting smaller points of interest?
*** '''Chartin' Charles McAtless:''' Well, you'll likely spot some interesting things in the sea and on some of the less explored islands that you find whilst out sailing.
*** '''Chartin' Charles McAtless:''' Charting these things is simple. All you need to do is just make a note of them as you find them!
*** {{tbox|Many points of interest don't require any tools to chart. Just interact with them from your boat or while on foot when close enough to them.}}
*** {{tact|other}}
** {{topt|Can you tell me about charting larger points of interest?}}
*** '''Player:''' Can you tell me about charting larger points of interest?
*** '''Chartin' Charles McAtless:''' Ah, for them, you'll want to find a good spot and use a spyglass to take it all in.
*** '''Player:''' But how do I know where a good spot is?
*** '''Chartin' Charles McAtless:''' That can take a bit of practice, but if you pay close attention, you might find some very subtle, definitely not obvious signs of where the best places are...
*** {{tbox|pic=Spyglass detail.png|The spyglass can be used to chart larger points of interest. You can do so either from your boat or while on foot. Keep an eye out for the sparkly white circles that show where a spyglass can be used.}}
*** {{tact|other}}
** {{topt|Can you tell me about drink crates?}}
*** '''Player:''' Can you tell me about drink crates?
*** {{tcond|If the player has not completed Prying Times:}}
**** '''Chartin' Charles McAtless:''' They're a bit of an interesting one. It's been argued that they're not actually completely essential for charting the sea, but Steve thinks otherwise. Probably best you talk to him if you want to know more.
**** {{tbox|pic=Crowbar detail.png|You need to complete the Prying Times quest to learn about drink crates.}}
*** {{tcond|If the player has completed Prying Times:}}
**** '''Chartin' Charles McAtless:''' They're a bit of an interesting one. On your travels, you may spot some sealed crates floating in the sea.
**** '''Chartin' Charles McAtless:''' Once you find one, just pry it open with your crowbar. If you're lucky, there will be a refreshing beverage inside for you to try.
**** '''Chartin' Charles McAtless:''' Be careful though, as some of them can be a tinge on the ripe side...
**** '''Player:''' I must admit, I'm not totally sure what these crates have to do with charting...
**** '''Chartin' Charles McAtless:''' Yes, that opinion has come up before. However, according to Steve, it's an unwritten rule in this world that alcohol is the key to solving all problems.
**** '''Chartin' Charles McAtless:''' It's also been said that these crates add a bit of much needed danger to the whole charting effort.
**** '''Player:''' I see...
**** {{tbox|pic=Crowbar detail.png|Floating crates of drink can be found at sea and pried open with a crowbar. Once open, you can sample what you find inside. However, take care, for expired alcohol can be dangerous...}}
*** {{tact|other}}
** {{topt|Can you tell me about tracking currents?}}
*** '''Player:''' Can you tell me about tracking currents?
*** '''Chartin' Charles McAtless:''' Absolutely! Understanding the various currents around the seas is essential. As you sail around, you'll likely spot many currents of potential interest.
*** {{tcond|If the player has not completed Current Affairs:}}
**** '''Player:''' But once I spot them, how do I track them?
**** '''Chartin' Charles McAtless:''' Ah, for that, you'll need the right tool. Well, I suppose in this case, it's less of a tool and more of a friend.
**** '''Player:''' What do you mean?
**** '''Chartin' Charles McAtless:''' It will probably make more sense if you head out and discover the art of tracking currents for yourself!
**** '''Chartin' Charles McAtless:''' We had someone passing through recently who said that Arhein in Catherby was looking to track some currents. I'd suggest you go and speak to him.
**** {{tbox|pic=Current duck detail.png|You need to complete the Current Affairs quest to learn about tracking currents.}}
*** {{tcond|If the player has completed Current Affairs:}}
**** '''Chartin' Charles McAtless:''' To track them, you'll need to make use of your good friend, the current duck! Specifically, once you've found some currents you want to track, you'll want to let your current duck head out for a swim.
**** '''Chartin' Charles McAtless:''' He'll track the currents for you, so all you need to do is follow him wherever he goes. Once he's done, just pick him up again and let him share what he discovered with you.
**** '''Player:''' Is this really the standard way of doing this?
**** '''Chartin' Charles McAtless:''' Of course! I simply can't think of any alternatives!
**** {{tbox|pic=Current duck detail.png|A current duck can be used to track currents. To do so, find an area of circularly expanding currents and release your duck there. Then just follow the duck with your boat and collect it again once it stops.}}
*** {{tact|other}}
** {{topt|More options...}}
*** {{tselect|Select an option}}
*** {{topt|Can you tell me about checking sea depths?}}
**** '''Player:''' Can you tell me about checking sea depths?
**** {{tcond|If the player does not have 38 Sailing:}}
***** '''Chartin' Charles McAtless:''' Ah, for that, you'll need to go diving. However, you don't want to rush it. You'll need to make sure you're skilled enough for that sort of thing before you... dive in.
***** {{tbox|pic=Fishbowl helmet detail.png|You require 38 Sailing to learn about checking sea depths.}}
**** {{tcond|If the player does has 38 Sailing:}}
***** '''Chartin' Charles McAtless:''' Ah, for that, you'll need to go diving. Doing so will let you take a record of the sea depth, but it's also great for learning more about the local underwater flora and fauna.
***** '''Chartin' Charles McAtless:''' However, I wouldn't reccomend{{sic}} going it alone. Fortunately, a lot of mermaids have been popping up recently, interested in the extra sea traffic.
***** '''Chartin' Charles McAtless:''' I hear they will guide you for a price, and for some inexplicable reason, that price seems to be solving a word-based puzzle for them.
***** '''Player:''' A puzzle?
***** '''Chartin' Charles McAtless:''' Indeed, so get your thinking cap on... under your diving gear of course. It's very important you don't forget that.
***** {{tbox|pic=Fishbowl helmet detail.png|To check sea depths, you'll need to find a mermaid in the ocean, don some diving gear and then answer her puzzle. She'll then guide you down to the bottom of the sea for you to document your findings.}}
**** {{tact|other}}
*** {{topt|Can you tell me about tracking weather patterns?}}
**** '''Player:''' Can you tell me about tracking weather patterns?
**** {{tcond|If the player does not have 57 Sailing:}}
***** '''Chartin' Charles McAtless:''' Well, all good captains need to have a strong understanding of the weather out at sea. However, it requires a fair bit of skill to do it well. I'd suggest you wait until you're more experienced.
***** {{tbox|pic=Portable weather station detail.png|You require 57 Sailing to learn about tracking weather patterns.}}
**** {{tcond|If the player has 57 Sailing:}}
***** '''Chartin' Charles McAtless:''' Of course! All good captains need to have a strong understanding of the weather out at sea. However, to do it well, you'll probably want to enlist the help of a meteorologist.
***** '''Player:''' Where can I find one of those?
***** '''Chartin' Charles McAtless:''' Well, it's a bit of an odd one, but I've been told there's a troll who has started working as one recently.
***** '''Player:''' A troll?
***** '''Chartin' Charles McAtless:''' Indeed. It's a bit unusual, but who am I to judge! Anyway, apparently she's aquired a portable weather station, a very fine piece of equipment for measuring weather data.
***** '''Chartin' Charles McAtless:''' If you come across this troll, she'll hopefully allow you to use this weather station for yourself.
***** '''Player:''' And how is it used?
***** '''Chartin' Charles McAtless:''' Well, what you'll find is that the wind typically blows in large circles. What you need to do is find the middle of this circle, or the eye as we often call it.
***** '''Chartin' Charles McAtless:''' You can use the weather station to work out the wind direction. If you follow it for a bit, you should be able to work out which way the circle is curving, and from that, you should be able to find the eye.
***** '''Chartin' Charles McAtless:''' Just remember not to keep following the wind forever, or you'll just keep going around in circles!
***** '''Chartin' Charles McAtless:''' Anyway, once you reach the eye, you can use the weather station to take the readings you need. After that, just make sure to return the weather station to the troll.
***** {{tbox|pic=Portable weather station detail.png|To track weather patterns, you'll need to find the troll meteorologist, take her portable weather station and use it to find the eye of a circular wind storm. Once there, you can use the weather station to record your data.}}
**** {{tact|other}}
*** {{topt|Let's talk about something else.}}
**** '''Player:''' Let's talk about something else.
**** '''Chartin' Charles McAtless:''' Very well.
**** {{tact|initial}}
*** {{topt|Previous options...}}
