Transcript:Dominic Onion.wikitext:
{{Transcript|npc}}

==Standard dialogue==
===If the player has no dream prepared in the vial===
* '''Dominic Onion:''' Welcome to the Nightmare Zone! Would you like me to create a dream for you?
* {{topt|Who are you?}}
** '''Player:''' Who are you?
** '''Dominic Onion:''' My name's Dominic Onion but you can call me Dom, or Mr Onion.
** '''Player:''' Mr Oni...Dom, how did you get that name?
** '''Dominic Onion:''' Well that's a long story...but I can tell you that it involved my parents, 3 blurberry specials, and a chinchompa.
** '''Player:''' ...and a chinchompa?
** '''Dominic Onion:''' Oh yes, Nigel played a crucial role in the whole debacle. It's all very amusing now that I think back to it.
** '''Player:''' Right...
** '''Dominic Onion:''' Good times...
** {{tact|initial}}
* {{topt|What is this place?}}
** '''Player:''' What is this place?
** '''Dominic Onion:''' This is the Nightmare Zone!
** '''Player:''' Wwwwhat?!
** '''Dominic Onion:''' Don't worry, it's not as bad as it sounds...most of the time.
** '''Player:''' That's comforting.
** '''Dominic Onion:''' Truth be told, that name wasn't my first choice, it's what the local folk have been calling it and so it sort of stuck.
** '''Dominic Onion:''' My original plan came to me in a vivid dream when I was younger you see, I saw myself running a successful business from a great structure in a strange land.
** '''Dominic Onion:''' Well, I say strange, but I'd never left Lunar Isle at the time and this place was very hot and dry, unlike anything I'd seen before.
** '''Dominic Onion:''' When I told my father about the dream he laughed and said I should become a banker like him and his father before him but in that moment I knew that it wasn't the life for me.
** '''Dominic Onion:''' I had to find out what this dream meant and if it was a vision of the future or not.
** '''Dominic Onion:''' Growing up, I studied hard to find out more about magic, especially oneiromancy and the interpretation of dreams.
** '''Dominic Onion:''' Having learned as much as I could on Lunar Isle I set out to find and learn from other great wizards I'd heard of in stories as a child.
** '''Dominic Onion:''' I set off to travel the world, discovering more about dreams to enable me to understand the dream I'd had as a child.
** '''Dominic Onion:''' I needed to know what this dream meant and if it was truly a vision of the future.
** '''Dominic Onion:''' If so I knew I had to try and find this location and build the huge tower I saw.
** '''Dominic Onion:''' I was going to call it 'Dom Onion's Tower', but I've not found this strange place or gathered enough money to build it just yet.
** '''Dominic Onion:''' That's why I've setup this small business venture in the mean time selling dreams to people. I just need a big enough crowd to kickstart my business.
** '''Dominic Onion:''' It's all part of my five year plan, and who knows, perhaps my dream will come true; I'll discover this place and build Dom Onion's Tower!
** {{tact|initial}}
* {{topt|Can you tell me about the dreams?}}
** '''Player:''' Can you tell me about the dreams?
** '''Dominic Onion:''' Certainly. I can delve into your memories and search for the key events that have affected you on your adventures.
** '''Dominic Onion:''' I then take the essence of these memories and put that in the vial you see on the plinth.
** '''Dominic Onion:''' I imbue a bit of magic, then give the vial a bit of a shake, and when you drink it you'll be able to re-live an encounter close to the original.
** '''Dominic Onion:''' Don't worry though, when you're in a dream, you're perfectly safe even if it does seem very real.
** '''Dominic Onion:''' If you sucessfully{{sic}} overcome the dream or die trying, you'll leave the dream state and return to normal with your grey matter and appendages intact.
** '''Player:''' Are all dreams the same or are there different options?
** '''Dominic Onion:''' Oh no, they can vary wildly! You can choose from one of three main options.
** '''Dominic Onion:''' Firstly, I can create a one-on-one encounter with an adversary you've defeated in your adventures. People like to practice in these dreams.
** '''Dominic Onion:''' Then there's a sort of Endurance dream, where you face enemies in encounter after encounter, and try to survive to the end.
** '''Dominic Onion:''' And finally there's something I like to call a Rumble, where you face multiple adversaries at the same time. I imbue a bit more magic and shake the vial harder to create that one!
** '''Dominic Onion:''' You can invite friends to fight alongside you in a Rumble dream. Once I've set up the dream for you, step into the enclosure and invite up to 4 friends.
** '''Dominic Onion:''' For the Endurance and Rumble dreams, I charge a fee for my work. I don't like handling the money directly, so instead I've set up a secure coffer.
** '''Dominic Onion:''' After you've asked me to set up a dream, put some money in my coffer. I'll deduct the fee from the coffer when you start the dream.
** '''Dominic Onion:''' There's a red vial on the other plinth. Your friends can drink from it to enter your dream as a spectator to observe your progress.
** '''Dominic Onion:''' Finally here's one other option you get, and that's how difficult the encounters are. As well as the normal dreams, the bravest adventurers can choose a harder version*.
** *Terms and conditions apply: Mr Onion, henceforth known as Dom, cannot be held liable for accidental loss of limbs (yours or otherwise) and or psychological damage as a result of entering the Nightmare Zone. Please note there is a strict no-refunds policy, and all dream purchases are final.
** {{tact|initial}}
* {{topt|Can I choose a dream?}}
** '''Player:''' Can I choose a dream?
** '''Dominic Onion:''' Certainly. You can practice for free, but the larger dreams require more skill to imbue the potions and so there's a fee for those.
** {{tselect|Which dream would you like to experience?}}
** {{topt|Practice}}
