* {{topt|Can you give me any farming advice?}}
** '''Player:''' Can you give me any farming advice?
** {{trandom}}
** {{topt|Dialogue 1}}
*** '''Fayeth:''' The only way to cure a bush or tree of disease is to prune away the diseased leaves with a pair of secateurs. For all other crops I would just apply some plant-cure.
** {{topt|Dialogue 2}}
*** '''Fayeth:''' Don't just throw away your weeds after you've raked a patch - put them in a compost bin and make some compost.
** {{topt|Dialogue 3}}
*** '''Fayeth:''' There are many Farming areas out there. I know of Elstan's area near Falador, Dantaera's area near Catherby, Kragen's area near Ardougne, Lyra's area in Morytania, Marisi's area in Hosidius and Alan's area in the Farming Guild. That said, I'm sure there's plenty more that I don't know about.
** {{topt|Dialogue 4}}
*** '''Fayeth:''' Supercompost is far better than normal compost, but more expensive to make. You need to rot the right type of item; show me and item, and I'll tell you if it's super-compostable or not.
** {{topt|Dialogue 5}}
*** '''Fayeth:''' There is a special patch for growing Belladonna - I believe that it is somewhere near Draynor Manor, where the ground is a tad 'unblessed'.
** {{topt|Dialogue 6}}
*** '''Fayeth:''' If you want to grow fruit trees you could try a few places: Catherby, Brimhaven, Gnome Stronghold and the Farming Guild all have fruit tree patches.
** {{topt|Dialogue 7}}
*** '''Fayeth:''' You don't have tp buy all your plantpots you know, you can make them yourself on a pottery wheel. If you're good enough at crafting, that is.
** {{topt|Dialogue 8}}
*** '''Fayeth:''' You can put up to five tomatoes, strawberries, apples, bananas or oranges into a fruit basket, although you can't have a mix in the same basket.
** {{topt|Dialogue 9}}
*** '''Fayeth:''' Hops are good for brewing ales. I believe there's a brewery up in Keldagrim somewhere, and I've heard rumours that a place called Phasmatys used to be good for that type of thing. 'Fore they all died, of course.
** {{topt|Dialogue 10}}
*** '''Fayeth:''' Applying compost to a patch will not only reduce the chance that your crops will get diseased, but you will also grow more crops to harvest.
** {{topt|Dialogue 11}}
*** '''Fayeth:''' You can put up to ten potatoes, cabbages or onions in vegetable sacks, although you can't have a mix in the same sack.
** {{topt|Dialogue 12}}
*** '''Fayeth:''' You can fill plantpots with soil from  any empty patch, if you have a gardening trowel.
** {{topt|Dialogue 13}}
*** '''Fayeth:''' Vegetables, hops and flowers need constant watering - if you ignore my advice, you will sooner or later find yourself in possession of a dead farming patch.
** {{topt|Dialogue 14}}
*** '''Fayeth:''' You can buy all the farming tools from farming shops, which can be found close to the allotments.
** {{topt|Dialogue 15}}
*** '''Fayeth:''' If you want to make your own sacks and baskets you'll need to use the loom that's near the Farming shop in Falador. If you're good enough at crafting, that is.
** {{topt|Dialogue 16}}
*** '''Fayeth:''' Bittercap mushrooms can only be grown in a special patch in Morytania, near the Mort Myre swamp. There the ground is especially dank and suited to growing poisonous fungii.
** {{topt|Dialogue 17}}
*** '''Fayeth:''' Tree seeds must be grown in a plantpot of soil into a sapling, and then transferred to a tree patch to continue growing to adulthood.
** {{tact|initial}}
