** {{topt|How can I improve my chances of making a capture?}}
*** '''Player:''' How can I improve my chances of making a capture?
*** '''Hunting expert:''' There are four key factors that will affect your chances: what bait you use, how close to the trap you are, your appearance and your smell.
*** {{topt|How does bait help?}}
**** '''Player:''' How does bait help?
**** '''Hunting expert:''' Unfortunately, creatures don't just jump into traps for the fun of it nearly as often as we as Hunters might like. However, it is possible to improve those odds. If you can find the right bait to use on your trap,
**** '''Hunting expert:''' something your prey really craves, then hunger overrides fear and the creature is just that little bit more likely to bounce to its furry little doom.
**** {{tact|other}}
*** {{topt|Why is it important how close I am to the trap?}}
**** '''Player:''' Why is it important how close I am to the trap?
**** '''Hunting expert:''' However well you might be blending in, if you're standing with your nose pressed right up against your own trap, the poor little critters ain't going to go anywhere near it. So, you need to make sure you put
**** '''Hunting expert:''' a sensible distance - I'd say at least four strides - between yourself and your trap.
**** {{tact|other}}
*** {{topt|Why would the creatures care about my appearance?}}
**** '''Player:''' Why would the creatures care about my appearance?
**** '''Hunting expert:''' You're a human. From the point of view of a lot of creatures, you're big and scary. So, it'd be best if the furry little monsters didn't notice you. You need to blend in like the creatures themselves.
**** '''Player:''' And how do I do that?
**** '''Hunting expert:''' Easy, dress up like one of them. Even easier, dress up using the furs of the creatures themselves; then you're bound to get the colour right. And, I suppose, if you don't fancy just slinging a dead fur over your
**** '''Hunting expert:''' shoulders, you can probably get them made into something more appealing. I hear there are tailors in Varrock who are good at that sort of thing.
**** {{tact|other}}
*** {{topt|What's wrong with my smell!?}}
**** '''Player:''' What's wrong with my smell!?
**** '''Hunting expert:''' I'm sure there's nothing wrong with your smell...from a human point of view. But to your prey, any trap that you've set up will reek of human, and that's going to work against you if you don't do anything about it.
**** '''Player:''' So what should I do?
**** '''Hunting expert:''' You need to mask that lovely human scent of yours with something else. Smoke works well. Take a lit torch and waft it around the trap a bit. You'll quickly overpower most of the other smells around the trap.
**** {{tact|other}}
