Transcript:Ignisia.wikitext:
{{Transcript|npc}}

==First time talking to her==
* '''Ignisia:''' Welcome, [brother/sister/my child].
* '''Player:''' Er... Are we related?
* '''Ignisia:''' We are all related, [brother/sister/my child], for we are all children of the flame.
* '''Player:''' Okayyy...
* '''Player:''' So what is this place?
* '''Ignisia:''' You stand before the Doors of Dinh. Behind them lies the prison of the Wintertodt.
* '''Player:''' What's a Wintertodt?
* '''Ignisia:''' We do not know what it is. All we know is that it threatens to snuff out every flame in this land and plunge the world into eternal darkness.
* '''Player:''' Oh dear... We should probably do something about that.
* '''Ignisia:''' That is why we are here, [brother/sister/my child]. Ever since the Wintertodt was imprisoned, members of the Order of the Sacred Flame, or Pyromancers as we're often known, have stood vigil over this place.
* '''Ignisia:''' But alas, despite our best efforts, the Wintertodt is growing in power again.
* '''Player:''' Well that's just no good. Is there anything I can do to help?
* '''Ignisia:''' Our order searches tirelessly for a way to defeat the Wintertodt. Until we discover it, the Wintertodt must be held at bay.
* {{tcond|If the player does not have at least 50 [[Firemaking]]:}}
** '''Ignisia:''' However, I fear your abilities are not great enough to withstand the cold of the Wintertodt. Learn the ways of the sacred flame and then return to me.
** {{tbox|You require at least 50 Firemaking to take on the Wintertodt.}}
** {{tact|continue}}
* {{tcond|If the player has at least 50 [[Firemaking]]:}}
** '''Ignisia:''' Pass through the Doors of Dinh to the prison within. You will find the finest of our order channeling the power of the sacred flame into the Wintertodt.
