Transcript:Liliwen.wikitext:
{{transcript|npc}}

==Standard dialogue==
* {{tselect|Select an option}}
* {{topt|Would you look after my crops for me?}}
** '''Player:''' Would you look after my crops for me?
** {{tcond|If no sapling is planted:}}
*** '''Liliwen:''' You don't have a sapling planted in that patch. Plant one and I might agree to look after it for you.
*** {{tact|end}}
** {{tcond|If a sapling is planted:}}
*** {{tmissing}}
* {{topt|Can you give me any farming advice?}}
** '''Player:''' Can you give me any farming advice?
** {{trandom}}
** {{topt|Dialogue 1}}
*** '''Liliwen:''' You can buy all the farming tools from farming shops, which can be found close to the allotments.
** {{topt|Dialogue 2}}
*** '''Liliwen:''' Applying compost to a patch will not only reduce the chance that your crops will get diseased, but you will also grow more crops to harvest.
** {{topt|Dialogue 3}}
*** '''Liliwen:''' Supercompost is far better than normal compost, but more expensive to make. You need to rot the right type of item; show me an item, and I'll tell you if it's super- compostable or not.
** {{topt|Dialogue 4}}
*** '''Liliwen:''' Don't just throw away your weeds after you've raked a patch - put them in a compost bin and make some compost.
** {{topt|Dialogue 5}}
*** '''Liliwen:''' The only way to cure a bush or tree of disease is to prune away the diseased leaves with a pair of secateurs. For all other crops I would just apply some plant-cure.
** {{topt|Dialogue 6}}
*** '''Liliwen:''' Vegetables, hops and flowers need constant watering - if you ignore my advice, you will sooner or later find yourself in possession of a dead farming patch.
** {{topt|Dialogue 7}}
*** '''Liliwen:''' There is a special patch for growing Belladonna - I believe that it is somewhere near Draynor Manor, where the ground is a tad 'unblessed'.
** {{topt|Dialogue 8}}
*** '''Liliwen:''' Bittercap mushrooms can only be grown in a special patch in Morytania, near the Mort Myre swamp. There the ground is especially dank and suited to growing poisonous fungii.
** {{topt|Dialogue 9}}
*** '''Liliwen:''' You can put up to five tomatoes, strawberries, apples, bananas or oranges into a fruit basket, although you can't have a mix in the same basket.
** {{topt|Dialogue 10}}
*** '''Liliwen:''' You can put up to ten potatoes, cabbages or onions in vegetable sacks, although you can't have a mix in the same sack.
** {{topt|Dialogue 11}}
*** '''Liliwen:''' If you want to make your own sacks and baskets you'll need to use the loom that's near the Farming shop in Falador. If you're good enough at crafting, that is.
** {{topt|Dialogue 12}}
*** '''Liliwen:''' Tree seeds must be grown in a plantpot of soil into a sapling, and then transferred to a tree patch to continue growing to adulthood.
** {{topt|Dialogue 13}}
