==Giving him the tarnished locket==
===First time===
* '''Player:''' Does the name 'Philly' mean anything to you by chance?
* {{tbox|pic=Tarnished locket detail.png|You present the locket to the Lumbridge Guide.}}
* '''Lumbridge Guide:''' That locket! Where did you get it?
* '''Player:''' I found it in a magical rift. Does it belong to you?
* '''Lumbridge Guide:''' Not exactly... It's a long and sad story.
* {{topt|It's okay, I have time to listen.}}
** '''Player:''' It's okay, I have time to listen.
** '''Lumbridge Guide:''' Well, if you're sure then.
** '''Lumbridge Guide:''' It all started in my youth when I was part of the Order of Wizards. I frequently spent time travelling across Gielinor, which kept me away from my beloved who worked here in Lumbridge.
** '''Lumbridge Guide:''' Due to being apart, I would often send her gifts. This locket was one of them.
** '''Player:''' I see... I'm not sure I like where this story is going. How come I found the locket in a magic rift then?
** '''Lumbridge Guide:''' As I said, my research often kept me away from home. During one of my trips away, our house was robbed. My dear Thenia tried to stop them, but they took her life in return. The locket was taken in the robbery.
** '''Player:''' Oh my... I'm so sorry for your loss.
** '''Lumbridge Guide:''' I appreciate your kind words, but this was a long time ago. The pain of losing a loved one never fades, but in time you come to live with it.
** '''Lumbridge Guide:''' Anyway, after that I stepped down from the Order of Wizards. I now spend my days offering guidance to those who come through Lumbridge.
** '''Player:''' I'm still curious to know how it ended up in some rift. Do you have any theories?
** '''Lumbridge Guide:''' Well... where was this rift?
** '''Player:''' In an ancient temple. Most things in the rift came from the Abyss.
** '''Lumbridge Guide:''' The Abyss? I wasn't aware anyone had ever been to the Abyss.
** '''Player:''' They hadn't until recently, but the Z.M.I. found a way there.
** '''Lumbridge Guide:''' The Z.M.I.? But could that mean...
** '''Player:''' What?
** '''Lumbridge Guide:''' Oh, nothing to worry about. Just me being a silly old man. Tell me more about this temple.
** '''Player:''' It's called the Temple of the Eye. It was built by Saradominist wizards long ago to house a powerful artefact.
** '''Lumbridge Guide:''' The Eye?
** '''Player:''' You've heard of it?
** '''Lumbridge Guide:''' Only stories, of which there are very few. Still, I always believed them to be real. After all, why else would an eye be the symbol of the Order of Wizards?
** '''Lumbridge Guide:''' Ah, but that reminds me, I was not the first in my family to join the order. This amulet was passed down from generation to generation.
** {{tbox|pic=Amulet of the Eye detail.png|Phileas shows you an amulet.}}
** '''Player:''' That looks just like the amulet that led us to the temple!
** '''Lumbridge Guide:''' As soon as you mentioned it, I wondered if there might be a connection.
** '''Lumbridge Guide:''' The origin of this amulet was something I spent much time puzzling over when I was younger. I'm glad you have answered the question I couldn't.
** '''Lumbridge Guide:''' I'd be happy to give you this amulet in return for that locket. I have no use for it, but that locket is something which holds a lot of sentimental value to me.
** {{topt|Of course you can have the locket.}}
*** '''Player:''' Of course you can have the locket.
*** {{tbox|pic=Tarnished locket detail.png|pic2=Amulet of the Eye detail.png|You exchange the locket for the amulet.}}
