{{Transcript|npc}}

==Standard dialogue in East Ardougne==
===Before Plague City===
* '''Player:''' Hello there.
* '''Mourner:''' Do you have a problem traveller?
* '''Player:''' No, I just wondered why you're wearing that outfit... Is it fancy dress?
* '''Mourner:''' No! It's for protection.
* '''Player:''' Protection from what?
* '''Mourner:''' The plague of course...
* {{tact|end}}

==Standard dialogue at the Ardougne Wall==
===Before and during Plague City===
* '''Player:''' Hello there.
* '''Mourner:''' Can I help you?
* '''Player:''' What are you doing?
* '''Mourner:''' I'm guarding the border to West Ardougne. No one except we mourners can pass through.
* '''Player:''' Why?
* '''Mourner:''' The plague of course. We can't risk cross contamination.
* {{tselect|Select an Option}}
* {{topt|What brought the plague to Ardougne?}}
** '''Player:''' What brought the plague to Ardougne?
** '''Mourner:''' It's all down to King Tyras of West Ardougne. It started came back{{sic}} from one of his visits to the lands west of here.
** '''Mourner:''' Some of his men must have unknowingly caught it out there and brought it back with them
** '''Player:''' Does he know how bad the situation is now?
** '''Mourner:''' If he did he wouldn't care. I believe he wants his people to suffer, he's an evil man.
** '''Player:''' Isn't that treason?
** '''Mourner:''' He's not my king.
** {{tact|end}}
* {{topt|What are the symptoms of the plague?}}
** '''Player:''' What are the symptoms of the plague?
** '''Mourner:''' The first signs are typical flu symptoms. These tend to be followed by severe nightmares, horrifying hallucinations which drive many to madness.
** '''Player:''' Sounds nasty.
** '''Mourner:''' It gets worse. Next the victim's blood changes into a thick black tar-like liquid, at this point they're past help.
** '''Mourner:''' Their skin is cold to the touch, the victim is now brain dead. Their body however lives on driven by the virus, roaming like a zombie, spreading itself further wherever possible.
** '''Player:''' I think I've heard enough.
** {{tact|end}}
* {{topt|Okay then, see you around.}}
** '''Player:''' Okay then, see you around.
** '''Mourner:''' Maybe...
** {{tact|end}}

===After completion of Plague City===
* '''Player:''' Hi.
* '''Mourner:''' What are you up to?
* '''Player:''' Just sight-seeing.
* '''Mourner:''' This is no place for sight-seeing. Don't you know there's been a plague outbreak?
* '''Player:''' Yes, I had heard.
* '''Mourner:''' Then I suggest you leave as soon as you can.
* {{tselect|Select an option}}
* {{topt|What brought the plague to Ardougne?}}
** {{tact|above}}
* {{topt|What are the symptoms of the plague?}}
** {{tact|above}}
* {{topt|Thanks for the advice.}}
** '''Player:''' Thanks for the advice.
** {{tact|end}}

==Standard dialogue in West Ardougne==
===Before completion of Plague City===
* '''Mourner:''' Hmmm, how did you get over here? You're not one of this rabble. Ah well, you'll have to stay. Can't risk you going back now.
* {{tselect|Select an Option}}
* {{topt|So what's a mourner?}}
** '''Player:''' So what's a mourner?
** '''Mourner:''' We're working for King Lathas of East Ardougne. He has tasked us with containing the accursed plague sweeping West Ardougne.
** '''Mourner:''' We also do our best to ease these people's suffering. We're nicknamed mourners because we spend a lot of time at plague victim funerals, no one else is allowed to risk attending.
** '''Mourner:''' It's a demanding job, and we get little thanks from the people here.
** {{tact|end}}
* {{topt|I haven't got the plague though...}}
** '''Player:''' I haven't got the plague though...
** '''Mourner:''' Can't risk you being a carrier. That protective clothing you have isn't regulation issue. It won't meet safety standards.
** {{tact|end}}
* {{topt|I'm looking for a woman named Elena.}}
** '''Player:''' I'm looking for a woman named Elena.
** '''Mourner:''' Ah yes, I've heard of her. A healer I believe. She must be mad coming over here voluntarily.
** '''Mourner:''' I hear rumours she has probably caught the plague now. Very tragic, a stupid waste of life.
** {{tact|end}}

