==Before finishing Pandemonium==
* '''Rum-dashed Ralph:''' Ahoy there, sailor! Can't stop to talk right now, I'm afraid. You'll need to come back later.
* {{tbox|You need to complete the Pandemonium quest to fully access the Sailing skill.}}
* {{Tact|end}}

==First talk after completing Pandemonium==
* '''Rum-dashed Ralph:''' Ahoy there, sailor, and welcome to the Storm Tempor!
* '''Player:''' Welcome? This place doesn't look very welcoming to me.
* '''Rum-dashed Ralph:''' What do you mean? We've got the fresh sea breeze, the spray of the ocean water, a supply of the finest rum around, and one of the fiercest storms in Gielinor to contend with.
* '''Rum-dashed Ralph:''' What's not to love?
* '''Player:''' Yeah, it's contending with that storm that worries me.
* '''Rum-dashed Ralph:''' Aye, it's true that the storm's bested many a sailor around these parts. Still, that's what makes things so exciting! We Barracudas live for the rush, and we trust that our skills will save us from a trip to the locker.
* '''Player:''' But why? Could you not just take the safer route around the storm?
* '''Rum-dashed Ralph:''' Well, you see, there's value in sailors with skills like ours. Most common folk would think like you and avoid the storm, but that takes time, and as them merchants say, 'time is money.'
* '''Rum-dashed Ralph:''' But that's where we come in! Those merchant folk sail up to the south end of the storm, drop off their shipments to one of our boats down there and we make sure it gets up to the Pandemonium!
* '''Player:''' I see. That does make sense, but what's in it for you guys?
* '''Rum-dashed Ralph:''' Why, the thrill of the sport! Sailing isn't just about going places, it's about mastery of the boat, the pull of the sails, the feeling of the helm in your hand and the taste of rum in your mouth!
* '''Player:''' Sailing as a sport? How does that work? What are the rules?
* '''Rum-dashed Ralph:''' Fancy getting involved, do you? Well, we Barracudas have trials set up all across the sea where you can test your mettle against the clock. I'm in charge of this here trial, the Tempor Tantrum.
* '''Rum-dashed Ralph:''' The objective of this trial is to collect rum shipments and bring them here. To do so, work your way around Tempoross Cove, towards our boat to the south.
* '''Rum-dashed Ralph:''' While you're out there, keep an eye out for any lost supplies. You'll need to collect all of them to complete the trial.
* '''Rum-dashed Ralph:''' Sailing over rapids will give you a burst of speed! Try to go over as many as you can. The more rapids you go through in quick succession, the faster you'll go!
* '''Rum-dashed Ralph:''' The storm isn't going to make it easy for you. Those storm clouds are a nasty piece of work and they'll slow your boat down if they hit you.
* '''Rum-dashed Ralph:''' Keep a close eye on them. If they are growing in size, that means they are about to strike. However, don't let your guard down once they do, as they always strike twice!
* '''Rum-dashed Ralph:''' As you make your way around, don't forget your objective. You need to keep picking up lost supplies on route{{sic|should be 'en route'}} to our southern boat.
* '''Rum-dashed Ralph:''' Once you reach the boat, collect a shipment of rum from it and then make your way back here.
* '''Rum-dashed Ralph:''' Make sure you come back the opposite side of Tempoross Cove to the way you went, otherwise you're going to end up missing some lost supplies.
* '''Rum-dashed Ralph:''' If you can deliver all the rum shipments and collect all the lost supplies in the time given, you'll be awarded a Barracuda rank!
* '''Rum-dashed Ralph:''' Each trial has three ranks: Swordfish, Shark or Marlin. Each rank is harder than the last.
* '''Rum-dashed Ralph:''' For this trial, you'll be asked to fetch additional rum shipments and collect even more lost supplies as the rank increases.
* '''Rum-dashed Ralph:''' You can't attempt the next rank until you beat the one before it. You can also try unranked if you'd like to warm up beforehand.
* {{Tcond|If below 30 sailing}}
** '''Rum-dashed Ralph:''' That said, with your Sailing experience I'd suggest sailing elsewhere for now and coming back when you've learned a thing or two.
** '''Player:''' Thanks for the advice, I'll bear that in mind.
** {{tact|end}}
* {{Tcond|If 30+ sailing}}
* '''Player:''' I see. Do you have any tips or tricks for me?
* '''Rum-dashed Ralph:''' Sure do, sailor!
* '''Rum-dashed Ralph:''' First up, you're going to need a boat with at least an oak mast built in order to withstand the storm. Your boat's as good as a goner without that.
* '''Rum-dashed Ralph:''' Second, your boat will also need to have at least an iron helm to withstand the rapids, but provided you can withstand them, they'll provide a burst of speed to your boat.
* '''Rum-dashed Ralph:''' Third, avoid them lightning clouds! Even with a strong mast they'll still slow you down.
* '''Rum-dashed Ralph:''' Fourth, keep your sails trimmed to gain even more speed. This aint{{sic}} no shipwreck salvaging. Go fast or go home!
* '''Rum-dashed Ralph:''' Finally, watch out for those rocks. Hitting them will kill all of your boats{{sic}} momentum immediately.
* '''Player:''' Thanks for the advice. I'll bear that in mind.
* {{tselect|Select an option}}
* {{topt|I'd like to attempt the Tempor Tantrum.}}
** '''Player:''' I'd like to attempt the Tempor Tantrum.
** {{tcond|If the player is manning the helm:}}
*** {{tact|opens2=The Tempor Tantrum}}
** {{tcond|If the player is not manning the helm:}}
*** '''Rum-dashed Ralph:''' You should make sure your helm is manned before starting the trial.
*** {{tact|end}}
** {{tcond|If the player has crewmates on their ship:}}
*** '''Rum-dashed Ralph:''' For this Barracuda Trial you are not allowed to bring any crewmates.
*** {{tselect|Select an option}}
*** {{topt|Can you help me transfer my crew away?}}
**** '''Player:''' Can you help me transfer my crew away?
**** '''Rum-dashed Ralph:''' Yes, I suppose so.
**** {{tact|opens=Crew Management}}
*** {{topt|I'll come back another time.}}
**** '''Player:''' I'll come back another time.
**** {{tact|end}}
* {{topt|Can you tell me about the Tempor Tantrum?}}
** '''Player:''' Can you tell me about the Tempor Tantrum?
** '''Rum-dashed Ralph:''' Well, you see, there's value in sailors with skills like ours. Most common folk would avoid the storm, but that takes time, and as them merchants say, 'time is money.'
** '''Rum-dashed Ralph:''' That's where we come in! Those merchant folk sail up to the south end of the storm, drop off their shipments to one of our boats down there and we make sure it gets up to the Pandemonium!
** '''Player:''' And what do I need to do during the trial?
** '''Rum-dashed Ralph:''' The objective of this trial is to collect rum shipments and bring them here. To do so, work your way around Tempoross Cove, towards our boat to the south.
** {{tact|above}}
* {{topt|Who are you?}}
** '''Player:''' Who are you?
** '''Rum-dashed Ralph:''' The name's Ralph, Rum-Dashed Ralph. I'm a trial master for the Barracudas and I've been tasked with overseeing our operation over here by Storm Tempor.
** '''Player:''' Are there any benefits to being a trial master?
** '''Rum-dashed Ralph:''' Plenty! Nothing brings a smile to my face quite like seeing a young budding sailor work at their skills and prove themselves capable of overcoming the storm.
** '''Rum-dashed Ralph:''' Not to mention, the free rum recovered while doing the trial doesn't go amiss either!
** '''Player:''' What about those that fail?
** '''Rum-dashed Ralph:''' I wish them a safe journey to the locker.
** {{tact|other}}
* {{topt|Who are the Barracudas?}}
** '''Player:''' Who are the Barracudas?
** '''Rum-dashed Ralph:''' We're only the fastest, most competent, most skilled and good looking sailors to sail the seas! Our motto is 'Anyone from anywhere as long as they can sail.'
** '''Rum-dashed Ralph:''' Our goal is to work together and teach anyone willing the skills required to be a master sailor capable of overcoming anything.
** '''Player:''' Can I become a Barracuda?
** '''Rum-dashed Ralph:''' Haha! That's the spirit! Of course you can, but only once you prove yourself in our trials. There's a bunch of trial masters like me scattered across the seas. Best our trials and earn your spot in our ranks.
** {{tact|other}}
* {{topt|I'd best be off.}}
** '''Player:''' I'd best be off.
** {{tact|end}}

