* {{tcond|If the player has level 1-14 Smithing:}}
** '''Player:''' Can you teach me the basics of smelting please?
** {{tbox|pic=5084 detail.png|Look for this icon on your minimap to find a furnace to smelt ores into metal.}}
** {{tcond|If the player has no ore in their inventory:}}
*** '''Smithing apprentice:''' You'll need to have mined some ore to smelt first. Go see the mining tutor to the south if you're not sure how to do this.
*** {{tbox|pic=22571 detail.png|Look for this icon to the south of here, in the swamp.}}
*** {{tact|end}}
** {{tcond|If the player has ore in their inventory:}}
*** '''Smithing apprentice:''' I see you have some ore with you to smelt, so let's get started.
*** '''Smithing apprentice:''' Click on the furnace to bring up a menu of metal bars you can try to make from your ore.
*** '''Smithing apprentice:''' When you have a full inventory, take it to the bank, you can find it on the roof of the castle in Lumbridge.
*** {{tbox|pic=5080 detail.png|To find a bank, look for this symbol on your minimap after climbing the stairs of the Lumbridge Castle to the top. There are banks all over the world with this symbol.}}
*** '''Smithing apprentice:''' If you have a hammer with you, you can smith the bronze bars into equipment on the anvil outside.
*** '''Smithing apprentice:''' I'm afraid the weather over the years has rusted it down, so it can only be used to work bronze.
*** '''Smithing apprentice:''' Alternatively you can run up to Varrock. Look for my Master, the Smithing Tutor, in the west of the city, he can help you smith better gear.
*** {{tact|end}}
* {{tcond|If the player has level 16-28 Smithing:}}
** '''Player:''' I already know about the basics of smelting, got any tips?
** '''Smithing apprentice:''' I find it useful to stockpile my ore before smelting it in one go, or even do it on the way to the bank in such places as Al Kharid or Falador. But you can do it anyway you want, one load at a time is fine too!
** '''Smithing apprentice:''' Not too much can go wrong with smelting.
** '''Smithing apprentice:''' You will lose some iron when smelting that ore, but a Ring of Forging or the Superheat Item spell will soon solve that.
** '''Smithing apprentice:''' You should also investigate Keldagrim, the dwarven city, you may find better places to smelt your ore with friends.
* {{tcond|If the player has level 29-99 Smithing:}}
** '''Player:''' What do I do after smelting the ore?
** '''Smithing apprentice:''' Ahh you'll need to learn to smith. Go to Varrock, that's where my master, the Smithing Tutor, plies his trade. Ask him to teach you how to smith.
** {{tbox|pic=22574 detail.png|Look for this icon in the west of Varrock.}}
** '''Smithing apprentice:''' Smelt some ore and store it in the bank. Grab a hammer from the general store before you go too!
** {{tact|end}}

Transcript:Smoggy.wikitext:
{{Transcript|npc}}

==Standard dialogue==
* '''Smoggy:''' Are you here to make juniper charcoal?
* {{topt|Tell me about juniper charcoal.}}
** '''Player:''' Tell me about juniper charcoal.
** '''Smoggy:''' They use it in the blast mine, out near Lovakengj. It's powerful stuff, more volatile than the regular charcoal you get elsewhere.
** '''Smoggy:''' To make juniper charcoal, put some juniper logs in my furnaces, then set them alight. I'll keep an eye on it for a fee of 600 coins.
** {{tact|other}}
* {{topt|Tell me about yourself.}}
** '''Player:''' Tell me about yourself.
** '''Smoggy:''' Juniper charcoal is my trade, always has been, ever since my mum taught me. She's retired now, and returned to Lovakengj - that's where we're from.
** '''Smoggy:''' I just live out here in the Hosidius farmlands because it's handy for the juniper trees.
** {{tact|other}}
* {{topt|What can you do for me?}}
** '''Player:''' What can you do for me?
** '''Smoggy:''' For a small fee, I watch the charcoal furnace so that you can make charcoal here. Also, I do a great back- rub{{sic}}, if you're ever in the mood.
** {{tact|other}}
* {{topt|Have you got a spare tinderbox?}}
** '''Player:''' Have you got a spare tinderbox?
** {{tcond|If the player has a tinderbox in their inventory:}}
*** '''Smoggy:''' Yup, but I'll keep it for someone who needs it.
*** {{tact|other}}
** {{tcond|If the player does not have inventory space:}}
*** '''Smoggy:''' Yup, but you can't hold it.
*** {{tact|other}}
** {{tcond|If the player does not have a tinderbox in their inventory:}}
*** '''Smoggy:''' Sure, you can have it.
*** {{tact|receives=a tinderbox}}
*** {{tact|other}}
* {{topt|I'll be off.}}
** '''Player:''' I'll be off.
** {{tact|end}}

Transcript:Smokin' Joe.wikitext:
{{Transcript|NPC}}

==Standard dialogue==
===Before starting [[Ratcatchers]]===
* '''Player:''' Hello!
* '''Player:''' Hello?
* '''Player:''' Hey!
* {{tbox|Smokin' Joe ignores you.}}
* {{tact|end}}

===After completing [[Ratcatchers]]===
* {{tselect|Select an Option}}
* {{topt|Can you tell me where I would find ....}}
** {{tselect|Select an Option}}
** {{topt|Grimesquit and Phingspet}}
*** '''Player:''' Can you tell me where I could find Phingspet and Grimesquit?
*** '''Smokin' Joe:''' Ah, the sisters Grime, as strange a pair as you're ever likely to meet.
*** '''Smokin' Joe:''' You'll find them in the sewers of Varrock.
*** {{tact|end}}
** {{topt|Jimmy Dazzler}}
*** '''Player:''' Can you tell me where I could find Jimmy Dazzler?
*** '''Smokin' Joe:''' Ah, young Jimmy, he must be a made man by now. 
*** '''Smokin' Joe:''' I remember when he was a lad...
*** '''Player:''' Do you remember where to find him, too?
*** '''Smokin' Joe:''' Hrmph! His old waterin' hole was the Flying Horse in Ardougne.
*** {{tact|end}}
** {{topt|Hooknosed Jack}}
*** '''Player:''' Can you tell me where I could find Hooknosed Jack?
*** '''Smokin' Joe:''' That old brawler? Is he still knockin' about?
*** '''Smokin' Joe:''' Well, your best bet would be somewhere on the east side of Varrock. It's rough around there though, be careful.
*** {{tact|end}}
** {{topt|The Face}}
*** '''Player:''' Can you tell me where I could find 'The Face'?
*** '''Smokin' Joe:''' You'll find her in Port Sarim.
*** {{tact|end}}
** {{topt|Felkrash}}
*** '''Player:''' Can you tell me where I could find Felkrash?
*** '''Smokin' Joe:''' Ah, the boss herself. You'll probably find her in the Port Sarim rat pits.
*** {{tact|end}}
* {{topt|Can you tell me more about the pits?}}
** '''Player:''' Can you tell me more about the pits?
** {{tcond|If the player does not have a [[Rat Pits manual]] in their inventory:}}
*** '''Smokin' Joe:''' Here take this, you might find it useful.
*** {{tbox|pic=Book (Ratpits) detail.png|You are handed the rat pits manual.}}
*** {{tact|receives=[[Book (Ratpits)]]}}
*** {{tact|continues}}
** '''Smokin' Joe:''' What do you want to know?
** {{tselect|Select an Option}}
** {{topt|Do you have any pointers for me and my cat?}}
*** '''Player:''' Do you have any pointers for me and my cat?
*** '''Smokin' Joe:''' You should wear an Amulet of Catspeak. It will allow you to organise tactics with your cat.
*** '''Player:''' What would be the best tactic to adopt then?
*** '''Smokin' Joe:''' Well, that depends on your outlook, whether you're ready to risk your cat's life or not and how defensive or aggressive you want your cat to be.
*** {{tselect|Select an Option}}
*** {{topt|I will not risk my cat's life.}}
**** '''Player:''' I will not risk my cat's life.
**** '''Smokin' Joe:''' Well if that's the case then you're left with two choices.
**** '''Smokin' Joe:''' You can adopt an ultra defensive strategy, which increases your cat's hitpoints and defence but causes it to flee sooner. 
**** '''Smokin' Joe:''' Or you can adopt a less defensive strategy, which will allow your cat to stay in the pit for longer.
**** {{tselect|Select an Option}}
**** {{topt|I think I would adopt a very defensive strategy.}}
***** '''Player:''' I think I would adopt a very defensive strategy{{sic}}
***** '''Smokin' Joe:''' In that case you should tell your cat: 'Just take care of yourself, cat.'
***** '''Player:''' Thanks for your help.
***** '''Smokin' Joe:''' Do you have any other questions about the pits?
***** {{tselect|Select an Option}}
***** {{topt|I'd like to ask you...}}
****** {{tact|previous3}}
***** {{topt|No thanks}}
****** '''Player:''' No thanks.
****** {{tact|end}}
**** {{topt|I think I would adopt a less defensive strategy.}}
***** '''Player:''' I think I would adopt a less defensive strategy.
***** '''Smokin' Joe:''' In that case you should tell your cat: 'Stay in for as long as you can.'
***** '''Player:''' Thanks for your help.
***** '''Smokin' Joe:''' Do you have any other questions about the pits?
***** {{tselect|Select an Option}}
***** {{topt|I'd like to ask you...}}
****** {{tact|previous3}}
***** {{topt|No thanks}}
****** '''Player:''' No thanks.
****** {{tact|end}}
*** {{topt|I am willing to risk my cat if it improves my chances.}}
**** '''Player:''' I am willing to risk my cat, if it increases my chances of victory.
**** '''Smokin' Joe:''' In that case you are left with two choices.
**** '''Smokin' Joe:''' You could go for all out attack which will boost your cat's attack and strength, but weaken it.
**** '''Smokin' Joe:''' Or, go for a less aggressive stance, which will increase your cat's strength and attack to a lesser degree, but carries no defensive penalties.
**** {{tselect|Select an Option}}
**** {{topt|I think I would adopt a very aggressive strategy.}}
***** '''Player:''' I think I would adopt a very aggressive strategy.
***** '''Smokin' Joe:''' In that case you should tell your cat: 'Go berserk!'
***** '''Player:''' Thanks for your help.
***** '''Smokin' Joe:''' Do you have any other questions about the pits?
***** {{tselect|Select an Option}}
***** {{topt|I'd like to ask you...}}
****** {{tact|previous3}}
***** {{topt|No thanks}}
****** '''Player:''' No thanks.
****** {{tact|end}}
**** {{topt|I think I would adopt a less aggressive strategy.}}
***** '''Player:''' I think I would adopt a less aggressive strategy.
***** '''Smokin' Joe:''' In that case you should tell your cat: 'No guts, no glory!'
***** '''Player:''' Thanks for your help.
***** '''Smokin' Joe:''' Do you have any other questions about the pits?
***** {{tselect|Select an Option}}
***** {{topt|I'd like to ask you...}}
****** {{tact|previous3}}
***** {{topt|No thanks}}
****** '''Player:''' No thanks.
****** {{tact|end}}
** {{topt|What benefits does my cat get from training in the pits?}}
*** '''Player:''' What benefits does my cat get from training in the pits?
*** '''Smokin' Joe:''' It depends on what kind of cat you have.
*** '''Smokin' Joe:''' In the Keldagrim pits, your cat will grow wiser by gaining more experience.
*** '''Player:''' Thanks for your help.
*** '''Smokin' Joe:''' Do you have any other questions about the pits?
*** {{tselect|Select an Option}}
*** {{topt|I'd like to ask you...}}
**** {{tact|previous}}
*** {{topt|No thanks}}
**** '''Player:''' No thanks.
* {{topt|Can you show me to the rat pits?}}
** '''Player:''' Can you tell me where I can find the rat pits in Keldagrim?
** '''Smokin' Joe:''' Down the stairs into the basement of the 'Laughing Miner'. A grand waterin' hole it is. Just look for The Beast, you'll find it.
** {{tact|end}}

