Transcript:Snowflake.wikitext:
{{Transcript|npc}}
{{Transcript list|Snowflake|My Arm}}

==Standard dialogue==
* '''Snowflake:''' Thank you for getting our herb patches to work. Now Boulder can grow goutweed for my people, and they are very happy.
* {{topt|cond=If the player lost the [[Weiss fire notes]]:|Can I have another copy of that book?}}
** '''Player:''' Can I have another copy of that book?
** '''Snowflake:''' Yes, I have another copy for you.
** {{tbox|pic=Weiss fire notes detail.png|Snowflake gives you another tatty book of Odd Mushroom's writings.}}
** '''Player:''' Thanks.
** {{tact|other}}
* {{topt|How are you two doing?}}
** '''Player:''' How are you two doing?
** '''My Arm:''' Snowflake an' My Arm very happy. Maybe new herbie patch not da only place where new life gonna be growin' soon!
** '''Snowflake:''' Let's not get ahead of ourselves, dear! But the town is thriving; my people are much happier now they are no longer terrified of Father.
** '''My Arm:''' Dem trolls likin' da goutweed too!
** '''Player:''' That's nice.
** {{tact|end}}
* {{topt|Can you note this basalt for me?}}
** '''Player:''' Can you note my basalt for me?
** {{tcond|If the player is carrying basalt:}}
*** {{tbox|pic=Basalt detail.png|Snowflake converts your [item/items] to [a banknote/banknotes].}}
*** {{tact|end}}
** {{tcond|If the player is not carrying basalt:}}
*** '''Snowflake:''' You aren't carrying any basalt.
*** {{tact|end}}
* {{topt|I'll be off.}}
** '''Player:''' I'll be off.
** '''Snowflake:''' You will always be welcome back.
** {{tact|end}}

==When using [[basalt]] on her==
* {{tbox|pic=Basalt detail.png|Snowflake converts your [item/items] to [a banknote/banknotes].}}
* {{tact|end}}

==When using [[goat dung]] on her==
* {{tbox|pic=Goat dung detail.png|No thank you, [player name], I do not need more poo in a bucket from you.}}
* {{tact|end}}

==Treasure Trails==
===Master===
My Arm does all of the talking, even though the clue requires the player to talk to Snowflake.
* '''My Arm:''' Here, solve this.
* {{tact|receives=a puzzle box}}
* {{tbox|My Arm hands you a puzzlebox!}}
* {{tact|end}}
====Talking again====
* {{tcond|If the puzzle is not solved:}}
** '''My Arm:''' That doesn't look solved to me.
** {{tact|end}}
* {{tcond|If the puzzle is solved:}}
** '''My Arm:''' Well done [player name]. Here you go.
** {{tact|receives=a [new clue/casket]}}
** {{tbox|You've been given a [new clue/casket]!}}
** {{tact|end}}

Transcript:Soar Leader Pitri.wikitext:
{{Transcript|npc}}
{{Incomplete|Out of date with latest update}}

==Standard dialogue==
* '''Soar Leader Pitri:''' Kuani! Someone's come to visit the birds!
* {{tcond|If the player has completed 10 rumours and has not claimed the free whistle blueprint:}}
** '''Soar Leader Pitri:''' I've spotted you working hard to help the guild. How would you like a basic quetzal whistle blueprint to help you get back here in the future?
** {{tselect|Take the free whistle blueprint?}}
** {{topt|Yes.}}
*** '''Player:''' I'd love one!
*** '''Soar Leader Pitri:''' You'll need to use the blueprint to craft a whistle from a willow log. Make sure it works for you. There's no standard size whistle nowadays.
*** {{tact|receives=a [[Basic quetzal whistle blueprint]]}}
*** '''Soar Leader Pitri:''' When you want to charge your whistle, be sure to bring some of those lovely meats you're gathering up here for the birds. If they eat well you'll get a lot more use out of them!
*** {{tact|continue}}
** {{topt|No.}}
*** '''Player:''' Not right now, thanks.
*** {{tact|continue}}
* {{tselect|Select an Option}}
* {{topt|Who are you?}}
** '''Player:''' Who are you?
** '''Soar Leader Pitri:''' I'm Pitri, though most of the others call me birdbrain.
** '''Player:''' On account of the...?
** '''Soar Leader Pitri:''' The birds, yes. I just feel so at home amongst them... Though I am more partial to cooked food than the raw stuff they get.
** '''Soar Leader Pitri:''' Is there anything else I can help you with?
** {{tact|other}}
* {{topt|Can you teach me about the birds?}}
** '''Player:''' Can you teach me about the birds?
** '''Soar Leader Pitri:''' Absolutely! Like many in Varlamore, we here at the guild use quetzals to help us move people and reports throughout the entire network of transport nodes.
** '''Soar Leader Pitri:''' We also have these handy quetzal whistles that allow us to call for one to take us back to the guild. They're pretty magical and work at very long ranges.
** '''Player:''' Could I get my hands on one of those whistles?
** {{tcond|If the player has not completed 10 rumours:}}
*** '''Soar Leader Pitri:''' Once you've become more settled in with us at the guild, absolutely.
*** {{tact|continue}}
** {{tcond|If the player has completed 10 rumours:}}
*** '''Soar Leader Pitri:''' Sure! I have a blueprint set aside for you to grab when you're ready.
*** {{tact|continue}}
** '''Player:''' So how do you motivate the birds?
** '''Soar Leader Pitri:''' Food, mostly. They're big fans of the raw meats that the hunters bring back with them. I'm worried they may be waiting to eat us, quite honestly!
** '''Player:''' Well, they're certainly big enough to try.
** '''Soar Leader Pitri:''' Is there anything else I can help you with?
** {{tact|other}}
* {{topt|cond=If the player has a whistle in their inventory:|Can you recharge my whistle?}}
** '''Player:''' Can you recharge my whistle?
** {{tcond|If the player has no raw hunter meats or Quetzal feed:}}
*** '''Soar Leader Pitri:''' Doesn't look like you've got anything I can feed to the birds here. You'll want to get some of the raw meats that the hunters bring back with them.
*** {{tact|end}}
** {{tcond|If the player has one raw hunter meat or Quetzal feed:}}
*** '''Soar Leader Pitri:''' Sure thing!
*** {{tcond|If the whistle is fully charged after exchanging raw hunter meat or Quetzal feed:}}
**** '''Soar Leader Pitri:''' Looks like the birds are all full for now. Make them work a bit before feeding them again!
**** {{tact|end}}
*** {{tcond|If the whistle is partially charged after exchanging raw hunter meat or Quetzal feed:}}
**** '''Soar Leader Pitri:''' There you go. Some whistle charges for you!
**** {{tact|end}}
* {{topt|cond=If the player has claimed the free whistle blueprint:|How do I get my hands on more whistles?}}
** '''Player:''' How do I get my hands on more whistles?
** '''Soar Leader Pitri:''' I can produce another blueprint for you, for a small cost.
** '''Player:''' What sort of small cost?
** '''Soar Leader Pitri:''' 500 coins. These blueprints are my art, and before you say anything, 'exposure' is the last thing I want out here in the savannah.
** {{tselect|Buy another whistle blueprint?}}
** {{topt|Yes.}}
*** '''Soar Leader Pitri:''' Here you go, one whistle blueprint.
*** {{tact|receives=a [[Basic quetzal whistle blueprint]]}}
** {{topt|No.}}
*** {{tact|end}}
* {{topt|cond=If the player lost their perfected whistle:|I've lost my perfected whistle. Do you have any spares?}}
** '''Player:''' I've lost my perfected whistle. Do you have any spares?
** '''Soar Leader Pitri:''' Someone found one just the other day and gave it to me in case someone came to claim it. Could it be yours?
** '''Player:''' It's possible? Can I see it?
** '''Soar Leader Pitri:''' Of course!
** '''Player:''' That notch in the tail, that scratch on the underside... Yes, it's mine! I can't believe it!
** '''Soar Leader Pitri:''' Here you go! I'm afraid it has no charges left, though.
** '''Player:''' Thank you!
** {{tact|end}}
* {{topt|cond=First time:|Can I get a whistle with unlimited charges?}}
** '''Player:''' Can I get a whistle with unlimited charges?
** '''Soar Leader Pitri:''' I see you already have a Perfected quetzal whistle, I can upgrade it for you at a cost.
** '''Player:''' How much is this going to set me back.
** '''Soar Leader Pitri:''' I don't want your coins. Instead, I would like 10,000 charges worth of food for the birds here. You can give that to me piece by piece as well if need be.
