Transcript:TzHaar-Ket-Keh.wikitext:
{{Transcript|npc}}

==Standard dialogue==
* '''TzHaar-Ket-Keh:''' Yes, JalYt-[caste]-Xo-[player name]?
* {{tselect|Select an Option}}
* {{topt|Tell me about the Inferno.}}
** '''Player:''' Tell me about the Inferno.
** '''TzHaar-Ket-Keh:''' TzHaar are born from eggs incubated in lava pools. When hatched, we retain memories. Memories and knowledge passed on from ancestors who returned to the lava.
** '''TzHaar-Ket-Keh:''' When TzHaar hatch, some memories are lost. Those about earliest ancestors are not retained. We experiment.
** '''TzHaar-Ket-Keh:''' This here was once our largest birthing pool. We use it for experiment. We increased the depth at which eggs are incubated. Over time, newly hatched TzHaar had more memories of lost history!
** '''TzHaar-Ket-Keh:''' But we kept pushing. We wanted answers, but we went too deep.
** '''TzHaar-Ket-Keh:''' Eventually the pool collapsed into a sinkhole. At the bottom we found some sort of ancient incubation chamber, from before earliest memories. We now call it the Inferno.
** '''TzHaar-Ket-Keh:''' We decide to experiment more. We take eggs from creatures in Fight Cave and incubate them down there.
** '''TzHaar-Ket-Keh:''' When eggs hatched, we see that it was not good decision. They were bigger and stronger, and fought each other for dominance.
** {{tcond|If the player has sacrificed a [[fire cape]]:}}
*** '''TzHaar-Ket-Keh:''' Instead of knowledge, we now have chamber of dangerous creatures, and they're not alone. Another being lives in the Inferno, one more powerful than any TzHaar.
*** '''TzHaar-Ket-Keh:''' We do not know where he came from. All we know is that TzKal-Zuk is hungry. Hungry for memories, memories beyond the Inferno.
*** '''TzHaar-Ket-Keh:''' We think his goal is the city itself. Lots of TzHaar memories here for him. Luckily, he is trapped in prison down there, and we are keeping him at bay by offering sacrifices.
*** {{tcond|If the player has not yet beaten the Inferno:}}
**** '''TzHaar-Ket-Keh:''' We fear he can't be defeated, but maybe we can hold back his creatures and keep city safe.
*** {{tcond|If the player has beaten the Inferno:}}
**** '''TzHaar-Ket-Keh:''' You, a mere JalYt, showed us he can be stopped though. Thanks to you, we still have hope.
*** {{tact|previous}}
** {{tcond|If the player has not yet sacrificed a [[fire cape]]:}}
*** '''TzHaar-Ket-Keh:''' Instead of knowledge, we now have chamber of dangerous creatures. It gets worse, but I don't know if I can trust JalYt-[caste]-Xo-[player name] with this knowledge.
*** '''Player:''' I like to think I'm pretty trustworthy. If you tell me, maybe I can help in some way.
*** '''TzHaar-Ket-Keh:''' I have one idea. If you sacrifice your fire cape to me, I can take your word.
*** {{tcond|If the player has a fire cape in their inventory:}}
**** {{tselect|Fire cape: Sacrifice it?}}
**** {{topt|Yes.}}
***** '''Player:''' Okay, I'd like to sacrifice my fire cape.
***** '''TzHaar-Ket-Keh:''' Very well, just hand it over.
***** {{tselect|{{colour|#ff0000|Fire cape}}: Really sacrifice it?}}
***** {{topt|No.}}
****** '''Player:''' Sorry, I want to keep it for now.
****** {{tact|end}}
***** {{topt|Yes.}}
****** {{tbox|pic=Fire cape detail.png|You hand over your cape to TzHaar-Ket-Keh.}}
****** '''TzHaar-Ket-Keh:''' Thank you, JalYt-[caste]-Xo-[player name]. You can enter Inferno now.
****** '''Player:''' What should I do down there?
****** '''TzHaar-Ket-Keh:''' The creatures down there are dangerous. If you can kill some of them, it would be very helpful to TzHaar.
****** '''TzHaar-Ket-Keh:''' But now you can be trusted, I must also give warning. Another being lives in the Inferno, one more powerful than any TzHaar.
